# 2. Deployment Section — Per-Environment Independence (Architecture)

## Background

The current Deployment Section treats all five environments (Test3, Test4, Stage-West, Production-East, Production-West) as a shared block. When a Force Refresh is triggered for any single environment, the entire Deployment Section enters a loading/blocked state — all environment tabs show "refreshing" messages and no other environment can be interacted with.

## Problem Statement

Each environment must be fully independent. Triggering a refresh on Test3 must not affect Test4, Stage-West, or any other environment in any way.

## Architecture Design

```
Current (Wrong):
  DeploymentSection
    ├── sharedLoadingState
    ├── sharedJobId
    └── allEnvironments ← blocked together

Required (Correct):
  DeploymentSection
    ├── EnvironmentPanel [Test3]
    │     ├── own jobId
    │     ├── own loadingState
    │     ├── own results
    │     ├── own connectionStatus
    │     └── own Refresh / ForceRefresh buttons
    ├── EnvironmentPanel [Test4]
    │     └── (same independent structure)
    ├── EnvironmentPanel [Stage-West]
    │     └── (same independent structure)
    ├── EnvironmentPanel [Production-East]
    │     └── (same independent structure)
    └── EnvironmentPanel [Production-West]
          └── (same independent structure)
```

## Functional Requirements

| # | Requirement |
|---|---|
| FR-2.1 | Each environment panel must maintain its **own independent state**: job ID, loading state, results, connection status, error state. |
| FR-2.2 | Triggering Refresh or Force Refresh on any environment must **not modify the state of any other environment panel**. |
| FR-2.3 | Multiple environments may run their Refresh/Force Refresh **simultaneously in parallel** — each creates its own backend job. |
| FR-2.4 | Switching between environment tabs must not interrupt a running job for any other tab. |
| FR-2.5 | Each environment's results must be independently stored in the DB and independently loaded. |
| FR-2.6 | The "Invalid Only" toggle must be **per-environment** — toggling it in Test3 must not affect Test4. |
| FR-2.7 | The backend must accept environment + namespace as **scoping parameters** per job request. |
| FR-2.8 | The backend must process each job independently — one job per (Team Key + Fix Version + Environment + Namespace) combination. |

## Backend Job Scoping

```
Job Request Payload (per environment):
  {
    teamKey:      "OC",
    fixVersion:   "26.7.4 (July 26 – August 1, 2026)",   ← full format, never abbreviated
    environment:  "Test3",
    namespace:    "com-att-oc-fmo-test3",
    jobType:      "REFRESH" | "FORCE_REFRESH"
  }

Job ID returned: unique per request
DB records scoped to: (teamKey + fixVersion + environment + namespace)
```

## Acceptance Criteria

```
AC-2.1
GIVEN the Deployment Section is open with Test3 selected
WHEN the user clicks Refresh on Test3
THEN only Test3 enters loading state
AND Test4, Stage-West, Production-East, Production-West remain in their previous state
AND their Refresh and Force Refresh buttons remain clickable

AC-2.2
GIVEN Test3 Refresh is in progress
WHEN the user clicks on the Stage-West tab
THEN Stage-West loads its existing DB results or shows a ready state
AND Test3 continues processing in the background

AC-2.3
GIVEN Test3 Refresh is in progress
WHEN the user clicks Refresh on Test4
THEN Test4 starts its own independent job
AND both Test3 and Test4 run simultaneously

AC-2.4
GIVEN Refresh has been run for Test3 and Stage-West on a previous session
WHEN the user opens the Deployment Section again
THEN Test3 shows its cached DB results
AND Stage-West shows its cached DB results
AND Test4 (never refreshed) shows an empty/ready state

AC-2.5
GIVEN the backend receives a Refresh job for Test3
WHEN the job runs
THEN it queries only the Test3 namespace
AND it does not touch records for Test4, Stage-West, or other environments

AC-2.6
GIVEN Test4 job fails (e.g., K8s cookie expired)
WHEN the failure occurs
THEN only the Test4 panel shows an error
AND Test3, Stage-West, and other environments are unaffected
```

