Currently there is no per-environment visual feedback during a Refresh. The user has no way to know that a background job is running or when it will complete for a specific environment.

## Functional Requirements

| # | Requirement |
|---|---|
| FR-3.1 | When Refresh or Force Refresh is clicked for an environment, display a **progress message within that environment panel only**. |
| FR-3.2 | The progress message must follow the same pattern used in the Generate Report section. |
| FR-3.3 | The progress message must include the Job ID for traceability. |
| FR-3.4 | The Refresh / Force Refresh buttons in the **active loading panel** must be disabled during processing. |
| FR-3.5 | Buttons in all **other environment panels** must remain enabled regardless. |
| FR-3.6 | When the job completes, the progress message is replaced with the results table. |
| FR-3.7 | When the job fails, the progress message is replaced with a clear error message. |
| FR-3.8 | The existing job polling mechanism (from Generate Report) must be reused — no new polling implementation. |

