# 6. Refresh Flow — DB + Kubernetes Only (Zero GitHub Calls)

## Background

The **Refresh** action is designed to be fast and lightweight. All component metadata (names, branches, stories, teams, exclusion status) is already available in the Components DB table. The only external call needed is to Kubernetes to get the current active branch and commit SHA.

GitHub must NOT be called during Refresh.

## Component Inclusion/Exclusion Rules for Refresh

> ⚠️ This is intentionally different from Generate Report behavior.

| Component Type | Refresh Behavior |
|---|---|
| Library | **EXCLUDE** — Libraries don't exist in Kubernetes |
| Helm Project | **EXCLUDE** — Not validated via this flow |
| System Excluded | **EXCLUDE** — Always excluded everywhere |
| User Excluded | **INCLUDE** ← Different from Generate Report. User excluded components still need deployment visibility. |
| Normal / Deployable | **INCLUDE** |

## Refresh Backend Flow

```
Step 1 — Validate Inputs
  Receive: teamKey, fixVersion (full format), environment, namespace
  Validate: cookie exists for this environment type
  If no cookie → return error immediately

Step 2 — Load Components from DB
  Query Components table:
    WHERE teamKey = :teamKey
    AND fixVersion = :fixVersion
  Fields to retrieve per component:
    - componentName
    - componentType
    - releaseBranch (already determined, stored in DB)
    - latestReleaseCommitId (new field — may be null initially, see Section 10)
    - scrumTeams (list)
    - stories (list)
    - exclusionStatus

Step 3 — Filter Components
  EXCLUDE: Libraries, Helm Projects, System Excluded
  INCLUDE: User Excluded (intentional — they need deployment visibility)
  INCLUDE: All normal deployable components

Step 4 — Kubernetes Calls (parallel per component)
  For each deployable component:
    Call Kubernetes for the given namespace:
      Retrieve:
        - K8s Branch Label (raw format: release-26-07-28-rel)
        - K8s Commit SHA (full 40-char)
  Use ExecutorService — parallel calls, not sequential

Step 5 — Branch Comparison (No GitHub Call)
  For each component:
    Normalize K8s branch → canonical format (release/YY.MM.DD.rel)
    Compare normalized K8s branch with releaseBranch from DB
    
    If branches differ:
      status = "Older Branch"
      
    If branches match AND latestReleaseCommitId is available:
      If K8s commit SHA == latestReleaseCommitId:
        status = "Valid"
      Else:
        status = "Needs Redeployment"
        commitsBeind = null (not calculable without GitHub in Refresh mode)
        tooltip = "Deployed commit does not match latest release commit.
                   Run Force Refresh for detailed commit analysis."
    
    If branches match AND latestReleaseCommitId is NULL (not yet stored):
      status = "Branch Valid — Commit Unverified"
      tooltip = "Release commit data not yet available.
                 Run Force Refresh to perform full GitHub commit analysis."

Step 6 — Persist Results to DB
  Save per component to Deployment Readiness table:
    - componentName, teamKey, fixVersion, environment, namespace
    - k8sBranchRaw, k8sBranchNormalized
    - k8sCommitId (full SHA)
    - latestReleaseCommitId (from DB — not fetched from GitHub)
    - deploymentStatus
    - validationMessage
    - lastValidatedAt
    
Step 7 — Mark Job Complete
  Update job status → COMPLETED
  UI polls and loads results from DB
```

## Functional Requirements

| # | Requirement |
|---|---|
| FR-6.1 | Refresh must only call **Kubernetes** externally. Zero GitHub calls. |
| FR-6.2 | All component data (branch, teams, stories, release branch) must come from the **Components DB table**. |
| FR-6.3 | K8s calls for all components in the namespace must run **in parallel** using ExecutorService. |
| FR-6.4 | Fix Version must be passed to the backend in its **complete original format** (e.g., `"26.7.4 (July 26 – August 1, 2026)"`) — never as an abbreviated or truncated value. |
| FR-6.5 | Branch comparison must use **normalized canonical format** for both K8s branch and DB release branch. |
| FR-6.6 | User Excluded components must be included in Refresh results but visually marked as "User Excluded" in the table. |
| FR-6.7 | If `latestReleaseCommitId` is null in DB, status must indicate branch match without commit verification, with tooltip explaining next steps. |
| FR-6.8 | Results must be persisted to DB and loaded from DB to the UI. |
| FR-6.9 | Total Refresh execution time target: **under 15 seconds** for up to 50 components. |

## Acceptance Criteria

