# 10. Components Table — New Field: `latest_release_commit_id`

## Background

The Refresh flow must avoid GitHub calls. To enable commit comparison during Refresh, the latest release branch commit ID must already be stored in the Components table, populated during the Generate Report phase.

## Problem Statement

Currently the Components table does not store `latest_release_commit_id`. Without this field, Refresh can only compare branches — it cannot validate whether the deployed commit is current.

## Database Change

```sql
ALTER TABLE components
ADD COLUMN latest_release_commit_id VARCHAR(40) NULL;

-- Description: Full 40-character SHA of the latest commit on the resolved
-- release branch at the time of the last Generate Report or Force Refresh.
-- NULL means the value has not yet been populated.
-- Populated by: Generate Report phase (when GitHub is already being called).
-- Used by: Deployment Refresh to avoid GitHub calls.
```

## Functional Requirements

| # | Requirement |
|---|---|
| FR-10.1 | Add column `latest_release_commit_id VARCHAR(40) NULL` to the Components table. |
| FR-10.2 | This column must be populated during the **Generate Report phase**, when GitHub is already being called for commit analysis. |
| FR-10.3 | The value stored must be the **absolute latest commit SHA** on the resolved release branch (including merge commits — same rule as Bundle 1 Section 5). |
| FR-10.4 | This column must NOT be populated during Refresh — Refresh reads it, never writes it. |
| FR-10.5 | If the column is NULL when Refresh runs, the status must be "Branch Valid — Commit Unverified" (see Section 8). |
| FR-10.6 | A DB migration script must be provided for this schema change. |
| FR-10.7 | The migration must be backward-compatible — existing rows get NULL by default. |

## Acceptance Criteria

```
AC-10.1
GIVEN the migration is applied
WHEN the Components table is inspected
THEN the column "latest_release_commit_id" exists as VARCHAR(40) NULLABLE

AC-10.2
GIVEN Generate Report runs for a fix version
WHEN GitHub commit data is fetched
THEN the latest commit SHA (including merge commits) is stored in
  latest_release_commit_id for each component

AC-10.3
GIVEN Refresh runs for the same fix version
WHEN the backend reads component data
THEN it reads latest_release_commit_id from DB
AND makes NO GitHub call to retrieve it

AC-10.4
GIVEN latest_release_commit_id is NULL for a component
WHEN Refresh runs
THEN the component status is "Branch Valid — Commit Unverified"
AND the tooltip instructs the user to run Generate Report or Force Refresh

AC-10.5
GIVEN the migration is run on existing data
WHEN existing component rows are inspected
THEN all existing rows have latest_release_commit_id = NULL
AND no existing functionality is broken

AC-10.6
GIVEN the migration script is reviewed
WHEN it is applied to H2 (current) and later PostgreSQL/Azure SQL
THEN it runs successfully without errors on both databases
```

